==Trivia==
*He is based on [[wikipedia:Dogū#Shakōkidogū|''Shakōkidogū'']], the most well-known variety of clay ''dogū'' figurines from prehistoric Japan.
**The word ''maru'' (丸) in Dogumaru's name can mean "full" or "whole" in Japanese. This may refer to how being attached to a horse statue's lower body has made Dogumaru complete again, as ''Shakōkidogū'' in real life are seldom found with all of their limbs intact.
*Since the end of [[Uncanny Legends]] involves the [[Great Ape Luza|origin of humanity]], Dogumaru may represent myths of [[wikipedia:Creation of life from clay|creation of life from clay]], many of which state that the first human(s) were made from clay.
*For a few reasons, Dogumaru could potentially be a nod to [https://youtu.be/Ne4qy1MwVDo Hanimaru] from the children's television program [[wikipedia:ja:おーい!はに丸|''Ōi! Hanimaru'']]:
**Both combine the name of an ancient Japanese clay figurine with 丸 ''maru'' (Hanimaru is ''[[wikipedia:Haniwa|haniwa]]'', Dogumaru is ''dogū'').
**As an enemy, Dogumaru's Japanese description mentions that he was thought to be a ''haniwa''.
**Hanimaru is usually seen with his horse ''haniwa'' Hinbei, while enemy Dogumaru's Japanese description states that he was mistakenly attached to the lower body of a horse ''dogū'' that had fallen beside him.

